{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00694 - MONDO_20320",
  "verbalization": "Daunorubicin is associated with Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation through a series of indication links that suggest a potential therapeutic relationship. The evidence indicates that Daunorubicin is linked to Acute Myeloid Leukemia Without Maturation and Acute Myeloid Leukemia With T(9;11)(p22;q23), both of which are subtypes of Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia. These subtypes are further linked to Quizartinib, a drug that is indicated for Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Daunorubicin to this subtype suggests a possible mechanism of action that is not yet fully understood, but it is likely related to the drug's ability to influence leukemic cell proliferation or survival. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship and underscores the need for further research to clarify the exact mechanism by which Daunorubicin contributes to the development or progression of Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation.",
